tool_args.old_string:
\paragraph{Formal reasoning with LLMs.}
LLM-solver pipelines~\citep{satlm, logic-lm, linc, fover-pei2025, lorp} and RL methods on solver feedback~\citep{polu2020generative, zelikman2022star, mellgren-prolog-grpo, logic-rl, deepseek-prover-v15, deepseek-prover-v2, deepseek-r1-2025} evaluate execution accuracy alone.
We use FOLIO~\citep{folio}, the only public NLI benchmark with both FOL and Prolog annotations.

tool_args.command:
cd /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/solver-trace-ablation/paper && python3 -c "
import subprocess
for p in [8, 9]:
    result = subprocess.run(['pdftotext', '-f', str(p), '-l', str(p), '-layout', 'main.pdf', '-'], capture_output=True, text=True)
    text = result.stdout.strip()
    # Check for Limitations and Ethics content
    if 'Limitations' in text:
        print(f'Page {p} contains Limitations')
    if 'Ethics' in text:
        print(f'Page {p} contains Ethics')
    if 'Checklist' in text or 'A1.' in text:
        print(f'Page {p} contains Checklist')
    lines = text.split('\n')
    if p == 8:
        print('  Last 6 lines:')
        for l in lines[-6:]: print(f'    {l}')
    if p == 9:
        print('  First 6 lines:')
        for l in lines[:6]: print(f'    {l}')
"
